nd ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111f643e-21fe-5850-a34c-7e75f866dffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288160} {:answer/id #uuid "5476c042-8711-54ab-b3d4-eadca3ea72e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288614} {:answer/id #uuid "6427fa83-3424-5638-881a-1b75c59158ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288737} {:answer/id #uuid "8d34a562-2280-5df3-b021-0fc8376c8ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x-\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288975} {:answer/id #uuid "f32241a6-5d82-568c-bcfd-3f92960cb105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x+\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288975} :answer-field/id #uuid "352c605b-c2ce-576c-94c4-6d4a6fa3df72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fabb0dc5-fadf-5950-bf52-26606893c541" :question/math-academy-id "q-2484" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsec} x$" :question/worked-solution "The formulae for the derivatives of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ and $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{arcsec} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x)+\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsec} x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)+\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x-\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdcb8335-d77f-5744-a62d-d1e124d9d3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296345} {:answer/id #uuid "7f99e84a-7088-47c4-b31b-db2302410090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}+\\frac{2x}{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21e2329-6733-5a78-a5e9-3327d19b15b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "75fdefb6-9025-5f7e-8537-d9b67757e76d" :question/math-academy-id "q-312358" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccot} x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9296d0-17e2-5a28-a674-eb8958050df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295344}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295344} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ddd26fa-15fe-5961-a3b9-0d7aba29d816" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "99fbb8d5-fc1d-5b4d-b999-a3255c91ff23" :question/math-academy-id "q-312364" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=5\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}+3)$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}+3)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{10(2)}{|{2}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({2}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{|7|\\sqrt{49-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\sqrt{48}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d669365-c1a7-59e0-93f1-eb14edcfb2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295435}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295435} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e600465-e185-5002-98a8-9f43960b3a79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbaf271c-e3b0-5a34-a834-13b6383c93b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296334} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbc0d1b-cfae-5acc-a1c3-73503eeef908" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a21be179-3e67-5f75-b560-ed7e4e4d7e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-312391" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x}\\,-$\n\n{{field-2}} \n$\\frac{1}{|x|{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}\\,x}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={x}^{2}+5$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x-({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}}{(\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x)^{2}}. \\\\  & =2x\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}\\,x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6323d4-42fa-5b0a-a662-4875e0f19a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297620} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb3f79-ae92-53fa-8e4f-156ba3393900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297682} {:answer/id #uuid "4da0246a-281e-5bbd-b144-5324057a41ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297874} {:answer/id #uuid "76bb75f6-7ed6-57dd-8f7b-90731f1a1dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298069} {:answer/id #uuid "e509e5c4-b769-5afd-a4b5-879400fecc6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297682} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7e2a43-6f12-5344-877a-8a1d3b75d45c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7013dfd6-3ee9-5a67-9438-689c7906b87e" :question/math-academy-id "q-31903" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(1)\\text{ } & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-6}{|{1}^{3}-6(1)|\\sqrt{({1}^{3}-6(1))^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{|-5|\\sqrt{(1-6)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{4\\cdot 6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{10\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{60} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01348264-a81e-56c3-895f-616259a8e027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297556} {:answer/id #uuid "0394f679-9a1c-5b87-94ed-5055b0ccff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} {:answer/id #uuid "50c36e45-828c-545f-9d7e-4d60c934349c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297888} {:answer/id #uuid "5a70b39e-a686-576d-b119-facfb9478e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297932} {:answer/id #uuid "fe851005-bb92-50a4-8f77-18e97f095b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298643}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c39276-107a-53e2-88ed-bb72cf785946" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1b0ce731-e82d-557a-b699-13d5ea673ea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31951" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{(6x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{{(6x-1)}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-12x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{4(9{x}^{2}-3x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d1446c-0422-5804-ab35-51c287ebd71b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3d8da40e-cfdf-5c60-a36a-cdb26f7bb8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341104" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+\\operatorname{arccot} x$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =2+\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d71143b0-47a4-55bc-833a-9a37cf1a0cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313670}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313670} :answer-field/id #uuid "42df9230-a42a-5643-ac02-c0cf183c1ecb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7de810d1-79ef-5695-be73-3f0627f342f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341115" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{arcsec} ({e}^{x})$ at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcsec} ({e}^{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)/2)}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09524a5a-9f20-5efe-91fd-6d5a59158a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312043}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312043} :answer-field/id #uuid "066f745e-563a-5525-a0d9-6cba6aa1ca90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f221de46-11bc-5772-aa56-5d0d13b544a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-341121" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc} (\\sqrt{x})$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arccsc} (\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2d52500-a992-5060-8249-a0e5114ed838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313765}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313765} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e24a99-cc76-5643-98c9-e83dbb7d91d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0bdae838-0b95-584e-856d-e0740682daed" :question/math-academy-id "q-341145" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,(\\sqrt{x}).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{1+x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0c4566c-bd79-5868-a603-18f0216abcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607} :answer-field/id #uuid "183d9fe6-f1f2-5fd2-b79e-60dbadd9be0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c596781e-b79d-5304-abff-1db8b7bfbe7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341146" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08831fa4-e925-511e-9c83-0ad4ccc9d162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{4}x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52cc14c-ea3a-52a9-8673-3631dde0a4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "88e0b1bd-ab5b-5056-934f-dc0524e7e997" :question/math-academy-id "q-341147" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d81e41-d413-5bdc-bac8-be87aebb35d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312778} :answer-field/id #uuid "283a6be5-839d-5ff0-9bb5-4cf7f3cc3f25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371c6c74-0468-5c9c-b71f-5ca91630b4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312419}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312419} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c25f5fd-d7bd-5f84-a472-da9da0020049" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "61288950-c35e-5f57-a1be-6d007672017d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341179" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{1}{|x|{(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\cdot \\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x-{3}^{x}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)}{{(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)}^{2}}. \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x}{{(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)}^{2}}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{{(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:answer/id #uuid "3ed6b8a7-489f-5243-a1ab-0833d4b3659d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{3x}|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{{e}^{3x}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339694}] [{:answer/id #uuid "72547bb8-80f4-5189-a664-31a103998d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340143}] [{:answer/id #uuid "778014a0-4d28-5cbd-bcfb-226c4ad315c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{3x}-1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{3\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{